      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi David, PTAL.",
      "revId": "4acc9bd1172d2be32b3a0474fd4892f7840bc6c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "57fd7e75_ca85c528",
        "filename": "libs/bssl/src/aead.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 28,
      "author": {
        "id": 1836235
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-28T11:25:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This feels like it\u0027s leaking BoringSSL-specific implementation details into outside world. Could we make this private to the module, and (e.g.) shift `AeadCtx::new()` to take `tag_len: Option\u003cusize\u003e`, with `None` indicating \"use default\" ?",
      "revId": "4acc9bd1172d2be32b3a0474fd4892f7840bc6c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "278a12f6_2ebe3cb1",
        "filename": "libs/bssl/src/aead.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 28,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-28T15:07:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I also considered this option, but it would result in two default values for `AeadCtx::new()`: `None` and `Some(AEAD_DEFAULT_TAG_LENGTH)`. That feels a bit confusing.",
      "parentUuid": "57fd7e75_ca85c528",
      "revId": "4acc9bd1172d2be32b3a0474fd4892f7840bc6c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9af04b70_ae9d115d",
        "filename": "libs/bssl/src/aead.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 28,
      "author": {
        "id": 1836235
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-02T07:59:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If `AEAD_DEFAULT_TAG_LENGTH` is private, then a user can\u0027t specify `Some(AEAD_DEFAULT_TAG_LENGTH)`.  But maybe an `enum` would be clearer:\n\n```rust\npub enum AeadTagLength {\n  Default,\n  Specified(usize),\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "278a12f6_2ebe3cb1",
      "revId": "4acc9bd1172d2be32b3a0474fd4892f7840bc6c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "17dcde80_4be70ab4",
        "filename": "libs/bssl/src/aead.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 28,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-02T08:38:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. I meant users can always specify `Some(0)`, but it will be the same with enum. Then an `Option` would be simpler in this case.",
      "parentUuid": "9af04b70_ae9d115d",
      "revId": "4acc9bd1172d2be32b3a0474fd4892f7840bc6c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6268b389_4b631cd2",
        "filename": "libs/bssl/src/aead.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1836235
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-28T11:25:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using this variant (with an embedded/inaccessible nonce) is likely to be limiting in a wider context; for example, it won\u0027t be compatible with COSE types that use `unprotected.iv`  (cf. all the examples in RFC9052 C.3/C.4)\n\nThe BoringSSL header also says:\n\n\u003e Warning: this is for use for FIPS compliance only. It is probably not suitable for other uses.",
      "revId": "4acc9bd1172d2be32b3a0474fd4892f7840bc6c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a29ae17_c3351bfb",
        "filename": "libs/bssl/src/aead.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-28T15:07:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e  it won\u0027t be compatible with COSE types that use unprotected.iv\n\nAlthough this function is not be ideal for general use, it meets our specific requirements in rialto, as we do not require direct access to the nonce. It is convenient to rely on BoringSSL for nonce generation and parsing instead of doing it ourselves like [1].\n\n\u003e this is for use for FIPS compliance only. It is probably not suitable for other uses.\n\nIndeed. David Benjamin also mentioned that this API was specifically introduced for ensuring FIPS compliance. However, it aligns with our use cases.\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Virtualization/microdroid_manager/src/instance.rs;l\u003d126;drc\u003d061478bca140291c354e8cf0d9d8aa9f47be8396",
      "parentUuid": "6268b389_4b631cd2",
      "revId": "4acc9bd1172d2be32b3a0474fd4892f7840bc6c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
