    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a2b1d8ec_a17367c7",
        "filename": "libs/bssl/src/aead.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 84,
      "author": {
        "id": 1836235
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-28T11:25:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`AeadCtx` doesn\u0027t really implement an AEAD currently, as there\u0027s no way to specify AAD.   \n\n(This in turn means it cannot be used for a `COSE_Encrypt0`, because even an empty \"external\" AAD gets turned into a non-empty AAD for the AES-GCM invocation, because of the `Enc_structure` stuff in RFC 9052 s5.3)",
      "revId": "4acc9bd1172d2be32b3a0474fd4892f7840bc6c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "350cb7dd_13053bba",
        "filename": "libs/bssl/src/aead.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 84,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-28T15:07:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The AAD is set up here [1] from the ad. I don\u0027t see an easy way to get this value out. Otherwise for the encrypted keyblob, we can pass a raw vector directly instead of `Cose_Encrypt0`.\n\n[1] http://google3/third_party/openssl/boringssl/src/crypto/fipsmodule/cipher/e_aes.c;l\u003d1065;rcl\u003d569168093",
      "parentUuid": "a2b1d8ec_a17367c7",
      "revId": "4acc9bd1172d2be32b3a0474fd4892f7840bc6c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
